The hmotor record is derived from the motor with a few changes which
are marked in the code.  Janet Tvedt found several bugs in the motor
record which are documented in the messages, below.  The bug fixes have
_not_ been applied to the hmotor record, though, some of my bug fixes
may duplicate Janet's fixes.  At some time, the bug fixes should be
applied into the system.

1) Sounds like a problem, but since the system is supposed to be
functional with all motors turning simultaneously, it shouldn't
overload anything.

2) I don't see this problem.  I may have fixed it myself.

3) I agree with what Janet has written, but I don't have any solution,
short of a complete rewrite of the device and driver.

4) This is not a problem because the NIRI motor power is controlled
by the hallstep record.

5) This has the potential to be very serious, but I haven't see in.

7) Currently I don't use the limit switch field, so this is not an
issue.

8) N/A (no encoders)

9) N/A (no encoders)

