	by hale.ifa.hawaii.edu (8.9.0/8.9.0) with ESMTP id LAA15391
	for <yamada@IfA.Hawaii.Edu>; Thu, 23 Jul 1998 11:22:48 -1000 (HST)
Received: from kiwi.tuc.noao.edu (kiwi.tuc.noao.edu [140.252.23.212])
	by noao.edu (8.8.8/8.8.8/SAG-11Jul98) with SMTP id OAA11130;
	Thu, 23 Jul 1998 14:25:36 -0700 (MST)
	(envelope-from tvedt@kiwi.tuc.noao.edu)
Received: by kiwi.tuc.noao.edu (SMI-8.6/SMI-SVR4-SAG05)
	id OAA13848; Thu, 23 Jul 1998 14:26:23 -0700
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 1998 14:26:23 -0700
From: tvedt@noao.edu (Janet Tvedt)
Message-Id: <199807232126.OAA13848@kiwi.tuc.noao.edu>
To: ajf@noao.edu, tvedt@noao.edu, yamada@IfA.Hawaii.Edu
Subject: Re: GEM5, motor record
Content-Type: X-sun-attachment
Status: RO
X-Status: 

----------
X-Sun-Data-Type: text
X-Sun-Data-Description: text
X-Sun-Data-Name: text
X-Sun-Charset: us-ascii
X-Sun-Content-Lines: 44

Andy and Hubert - 

I am no longer using the motor record.  I needed to develop a 
custom record to handle the unique positioning requirements of 
the GNIRS mechanisms anyway, so I incorporated what little bit 
of the motor record I needed into my custom record.  My new
record has a different name (Dstep, at the moment).  

I copied the OMS device support from the motor record.  I have
made a few changes to it.  I think the changes are backwards
compatible, but device support has some knowledge of the record 
constructs and so I'm not sure it can be used by other records.  
I have renamed it devDstepOms.c.

I think the OMS device driver is the only piece that can remain
common.  I have made some changes to it as well.  I addressed
these changes in an email to gemini-software last week.  Please
see the attached message.  One of the changes is trivial and
was not mentioned in the attachment.  I changed two instances
of "ID" to "IP".  The IP command is needed to support the position
maintenance mode and is interpreted as an ID by the OMS controller
if position maintenance mode is turned off.

Item 7 in the attachment refers to a section of code that I needed
to comment out.  I have never gotten a response from Tim Mooney
or Ron Sluiter on how to fix the problem correctly.  I have emailed
them at least 3 times about this and have given up.

I strongly recommend that you make the changes I identified in
items 1 and 2 to whatever version of the motor record you plan
to put in the distribution.  The driver in the distribution will
NOT work for me without the IP command and some resolution to 
item 7, but I can rename my version for now.

Janet

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Janet Tvedt, Engineering Technical Services     Internet: tvedt@noao.edu
National Optical Astronomy Observatories        Phone:    (520) 318-8388
950 N. Cherry Ave., Tucson, AZ  85719           FAX:      (520) 318-8360




